  "name": "Reese Drift",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "Detuned reese: Saw Stack in 6-voice unison (22 cents, width 0.6) on Osc A plus a 5-voice Saw Stack 7 cents sharp on Osc B, spread A left / B right, both through LP12s that the filter envelope sweeps open over about a second, a clean sine sub at the played pitch underneath and everything mono below 120 Hz. Play: long notes and slides around F1-C2 (halftime, DnB); overlap notes for legato glides. Tweak: Osc A/B Detune for the beating speed, Filter Env Amt and Decay for the sweep, Spread and Width for stereo size, Sub Level for weight. FX: Overdrive +6 dB with a Post low-pass at 5 kHz, multiband squash at 80 % depth (time 50 %) to pull the detuned beating forward, an EQ low cut at 25 Hz and -2 dB at 250 Hz, a slow 4-voice Chorus (wet low cut 200 Hz, 30 %) that keeps the sub mono, and a 10 % small hall. A slow Mod B and a random offset per note keep the beating from ever repeating. Macros: Detune widens the beating, Sweep opens both filters, Width spreads the stereo field above a mono sub and Grit pushes the drive and squash.",
  "category": "Bass/reese",
